  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve of Iraq soil fertility by Dutch water management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: This project has been cancelled, because of difficulties within the partnership.The project is initiated by Koop Watermanagement B.V. and its partner to provide the Iraqi market with both an own factory for drainage tubes and an organisation that will be able to install deep drainage in the saline soils of Iraq. The partners see this as an opportunity as the Iraqi government is financing (deep) drainage application as a way to revive the own agricultural production.The factory for the drainage tubes will be either established in Baghdad or Najaf. The drainage part of the company will have it base with the factory but the land where it will perform its business is situated around Najaf (200 km south of Baghdad) and further south. The total surface that will be provided with drainage is not known yet but the surface of saline soils is estimated at tens of thousands of hectares.Applicant Koop Watermanagement B.V. and local partner Al-Mubarak International Group are cooperating at the moment on a project to build a dam in the Euphrates river. For the project, they will establish a joint venture on a fifty-fifty share basis.The project will facilitate agricultural development in a large part of Iraq, this is a top priority of the Iraqi government. The project will also contribute to the industrial development of Iraq as it introduces the more advanced production process for drainage tubes.</narrative>
  </description>
